## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/scripts/build_macos_nosandbox.sh | ⚠️ important the new releasenosandbox configuration is consumed by no build path — ci is the gate cannot gate it the headline claim is orphan killed — real build configuration goal step 2 what actually ships is decided by the line above this comment flutter build macos release builds the release configuration and the no sandbox entitlements reach the app only via the script s point of use re sign codesign force … entitlements entitlements the gh 2039 hardened path a repo wide search finds zero invocations of configuration releasenosandbox in any workflow script or doc — xcode backend s contains release mapping is only relevant if something builds that configuration and nothing does consequences the configuration s buildability is asserted only by plutil lint string pins in the new guard test since ci never invokes the configuration ci is the gate is not true for this deliverable — a broken config would pass ci forever the realistic breakage vectors are exactly the unverified ones cocoapods per config xconfig generation for a configuration cocoapods has never generated and the deployment target floor that exists via the new appinfo xconfig pin only for the runner target — the project level clone carries no macosx deployment target so the flutter assemble runnertests targets resolve no floor under this config name the guard test pins structure not function green ci yields false confidence that the real build configuration works and goal step 4 topology inversion would naturally switch the build onto this never once built configuration suggested resolution either is acceptable 1 pin the inertness honestly — a guard assertion that the shipping script stays the sole consumer of releasenosandbox entitlements e g the script must not pass configuration releasenosandbox until a macos lane actually executes it plus a comment on the config block stating the configuration is structural until first executed or 2 actually consume it in a gated non release leg e g a config only adjacent or scheme less xcodebuild invocation on the macos runner before it claims to be real the shipped artifact itself is fine — the seal order fix and the ac3 signed set assertion are correct and well tested — this thread is about the gap between the real build configuration claim and the inert structure behind it |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | flutter_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj | 💡 suggestion the project level releasenosandbox clone carries a swift version line no other project level config has the pr describes this configuration as byte cloned from release via a mechanical transform entitlements pin swapped two deviations exist in the project level block 1 macosx deployment target 14 0 removed — documented and deliberate keeps the spm lane guard s 3×14 0 floor shape compensated by the new appinfo xconfig pin for the runner target fine 2 swift version 5 0 added — undocumented project level debug release profile carry swift version only at target level this is the only project level block with the key verified 8 occurrences in the file 7 pre existing all at target level behavior neutral today the target level clones already set 5 0 but it breaks the mechanical byte clone story and will trip any future shape guard that compares project level blocks fix delete this swift version 5 0 line so the clone is literal modulo the documented floor removal — no guard counts swift version occurrences verified so removal is risk free — or document why it is there |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

